OL,3,GNEWSAVictim begged robber to let him
OL,4,Asave dying dog photos
OL,5,
OL,6,FA robber who agreed to let one of his
OL,7,Fvictims save photos of his dying dog
OL,8,Fbefore he stole his phone has been
OL,9,Fjailed.
OL,11,FDerbyshire Police said Remar Junor
OL,12,Fcarried out three robberies and two
OL,13,Fattempted robberies in Littleover and
OL,14,FMickleover during a three-day period in
OL,15,FAugust.
OL,17,FOfficers said after being ordered to
OL,18,Fhand over his phone in Sunnydale Park,
OL,19,Fone victim begged to be allowed to save
OL,20,Fphotos of his dog as it only had months
OL,21,Fto live, to which Junor said: "Don't
OL,22,Ftell me that, why did I choose you?"
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
